  "stem": "The value of \\(y\\) is directly proportional to the value of \\(x\\). When \\(x = 12\\), \\(y = 30\\). When \\(x = k\\), the value of \\(y\\) is \\(2k + 1\\). What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "2"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Direct proportion: \\(y = cx\\) with \\(c = \\frac{30}{12} = 2.5\\), so \\(y = 2.5x\\).",
    "When \\(x = k\\): \\(2.5k = 2k + 1\\), so \\(0.5k = 1\\) and \\(k = 2\\). Check: \\(y = 2.5 \\cdot 2 = 5 = 2(2) + 1\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "k = symbols('k')\nc = Rational(30, 12)\nans = solve(Eq(c*k, 2*k + 1), k)[0]\nassert ans == 2\nassert len(spr_answers) == 1 and Rational(spr_answers[0]) == ans",
